    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nHeat released by condensing steam (m_s L_v) and cooling condensed water (m_s c (100 - T)) equals heat absorbed by cool water (m_w c (T - 20)).\n\n2. GIVEN:\nm_s = 2.0 g at 100°C, m_w = 50.0 g at 20°C, L_v = 540 cal/g.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nm_s L_v + m_s c_w (100 - T) = m_w c_w (T - T_w)\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Heat lost by steam: 2.0 × 540 + 2.0 × 1 × (100 - T) = 1280.0 - 2.0 T.\n2. Heat gained by water: 50.0 × 1 × (T - 20) = 50.0 T - 1000.0.\n3. Equating: 1280.0 + 1000.0 = (52.0) T.\n4. T = 2280.0 / 52.0 = 43.85°C.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 43.85°C\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nCondensed steam contributes to the total final mass of liquid water: total mass = m_w + m_s!",
